	(text "Use X7R for C17, C18"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 102.616 281.178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "29d1204d-ff90-48e5-b0e5-36cd6e4238ca")
	)
	(text "; ============================================================================\n; padne directives - KOI 8x8 daughterboard\n; rev: A30=+12V, C25 bulk, U9 AT21CS01, R18=2.7k\n; 2026-07-30: C23 moved +3.3V -> VDDA (now 1.1uF on the filtered node);\n;             R27 1.5 -> 10 ohm; L1 DCR 0.1 -> 0.38 (Sunlord GZ1608U601CTF)\n; 2026-08-05: OPA2333 input buffers U13-U16 added between the sense dividers\n;             and the AD7193 inputs (R28-R35 + C26-C33 AA filter); their\n;             quiescent supply current is now modelled. VREF is now driven by\n;             a VOLTAGE source at the REF5030 output - before this, VREF had\n;             0.505 mA drawn out of it (U20.1 + U11.7) with no source, so it\n;             floated and the solver reported \"Ground node current is not\n;             zero (-0.000505 A)\" and the reference net's IR drop was never\n;             simulated at all.\n; All designators/pads verified against daughterboard.kicad_pcb\n;\n; v3 CHANGE: the optional DAC-trace block is disabled. In v2 it injected\n; +50uA at the DAC pin and drew -50uA at the XTR pin of the SAME net, giving\n; each DACx net zero net current and NO resistive path to any reference.\n; Those nets' potentials were mathematically undetermined -> \"Matrix is\n; exactly singular\" -> every voltage NaN. A properly-referenced version is\n; at the bottom, commented out.\n;\n;   padne solve daughterboard.kicad_pro pdn.padne\n;   padne paraview pdn.padne padne_out/\n;   python3 padne_plots_v2.py padne_out/ results/          (all layers, 2x2)\n;   python3 padne_plots_layers.py padne_out/ results/layers  (one PNG/layer)\n; ============================================================================\n\n; ---- SUPPLY SOURCES (entering at the real connector fingers) ---------------\n!padne VOLTAGE v=3.3 p=3V3.1 n=C24.2\n!padne VOLTAGE v=12  p=12V0.1 n=C25.2\n\n; ---- ON-BOARD REFERENCE ---------------------------------------------------\n; REF5030 3.0 V output. Sourced at U10's own output/ground pins (NOT at the\n; VREF1 testpoint) so the reference current leaves the regulator pin and\n; flows through the real copper to U11.7 and U20.1, which is what the board\n; actually does. Without this the VREF net is a floating island.\n!padne VOLTAGE v=3.0 p=U10.6 n=U10.4\n\n; ---- DVDD filter path (AD7193 digital rail) -------------------------------\n!padne RESISTANCE r=0.38 a=L1.1 b=L1.2\n!padne RESISTANCE r=10 a=R27.2 b=R27.1\n\n; ---- IC supply currents ---------------------------------------------------\n!padne CURRENT i=4mA   f=U11.24 t=U11.22\n!padne CURRENT i=1mA   f=U11.25 t=U11.23\n!padne CURRENT i=5uA   f=U11.7  t=U11.8\n!padne CURRENT i=1mA   f=U10.2  t=U10.4\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U20.7  t=U20.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.5mA f=U20.16 t=U20.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.5mA f=U20.1  t=U20.6\n!padne CURRENT i=1mA   f=U8.16  t=U8.8\n\n; ---- INPUT BUFFERS U13-U16 (OPA2333 dual, 2026-08-05) ---------------------\n; Unity-gain followers between each sense-divider tap (CHx_B) and the AD7193\n; input, one dual package per two channels:\n;   U13 = CH0 (A: in 3, out 1) + CH1 (B: in 5, out 7)\n;   U14 = CH2 (A)              + CH3 (B)\n;   U15 = CH4 (A)              + CH5 (B)\n;   U16 = CH6 (A)              + CH7 (B)\n; Supply pin 8 = +3.3V, pin 4 = V- = GND (pin 9 is the DRB thermal pad, also\n; GND - use pin 4, padne skips via-centred thermal pads, cf. U20.17).\n; IQ = 17 uA/amplifier typ -> 34 uA per dual package. Scale if you measure\n; something different. The followers' OUTPUT carries no meaningful DC (they\n; drive 1k into an ADC input with pA-level bias), so only quiescent current\n; is modelled - see NOT MODELLED for R28-R35.\n!padne CURRENT i=34uA f=U13.8 t=U13.4\n!padne CURRENT i=34uA f=U14.8 t=U14.4\n!padne CURRENT i=34uA f=U15.8 t=U15.4\n!padne CURRENT i=34uA f=U16.8 t=U16.4\n\n; ---- EEPROM (parasitically powered through the 2.7k pullup) ---------------\n!padne RESISTANCE r=2700 a=R18.1 b=R18.2\n!padne CURRENT i=0.1mA f=U9.1 t=U9.3\n\n; ============================================================================\n; PER-CHANNEL BLOCKS\n;   XTR quiescent (pin5->pin9), pass current (pin5->pin6),\n;   SET-pin current (pin5->pin10) draining through the 5k to GND,\n;   external 800R load across both J1 fingers to the adjacent GND finger,\n;   sense divider as real resistances (100k top + 20k bottom).\n; Set i= to your real per-channel output current (3mA shown).\n; SET current = I_out/10 per XTR200 transconductance -> scale with i=.\n;\n; Measurement chain (since 2026-08-05):\n;   heater -> CHx -> 100k -> CHx_B -> buffer -> 1k -> CHx_V -> AD7193 AIN\n;                      |\n;                     20k\n;                      |\n;                     GND\n; The divider is unchanged and still carries the full divider current; the\n; buffer only removes the ADC's input loading from CHx_B. The accuracy-\n; critical gradient is still (divider bottom Rxx.1) vs (U11.10 AINCOM /\n; U11.8 REFIN-), because a follower reproduces its input in absolute terms.\n; ============================================================================\n\n; ---- CH0 : U0, R2/R6, SET R22, J1 A13/B13, gnd A14, buf U13A -------------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U0.5 t=U0.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U0.5 t=U0.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U0.5 t=U0.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R22.2 b=R22.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A13,J1.B13 b=J1.A14 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R2.2 b=R2.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R6.2 b=R6.1\n\n; ---- CH1 : U1, R10/R14, SET R19, J1 A15/B15, gnd A16, buf U13B -----------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U1.5 t=U1.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U1.5 t=U1.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U1.5 t=U1.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R19.2 b=R19.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A15,J1.B15 b=J1.A16 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R10.2 b=R10.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R14.2 b=R14.1\n\n; ---- CH2 : U2, R9/R13, SET R25, J1 A18/B18, gnd A19, buf U14A ------------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U2.5 t=U2.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U2.5 t=U2.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U2.5 t=U2.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R25.2 b=R25.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A18,J1.B18 b=J1.A19 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R9.2 b=R9.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R13.2 b=R13.1\n\n; ---- CH3 : U3, R1/R5, SET R20, J1 A20/B20, gnd A21, buf U14B -------------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U3.5 t=U3.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U3.5 t=U3.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U3.5 t=U3.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R20.2 b=R20.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A20,J1.B20 b=J1.A21 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R1.2 b=R1.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R5.2 b=R5.1\n\n; ---- CH4 : U4, R4/R8, SET R24, J1 A22/B22, gnd A23, buf U15A -------------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U4.5 t=U4.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U4.5 t=U4.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U4.5 t=U4.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R24.2 b=R24.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A22,J1.B22 b=J1.A23 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R4.2 b=R4.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R8.2 b=R8.1\n\n; ---- CH5 : U5, R12/R16, SET R21, J1 A24/B24, gnd A25, buf U15B -----------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U5.5 t=U5.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U5.5 t=U5.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U5.5 t=U5.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R21.2 b=R21.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A24,J1.B24 b=J1.A25 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R12.2 b=R12.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R16.2 b=R16.1\n\n; ---- CH6 : U6, R11/R15, SET R26, J1 A26/B26, gnd A27, buf U16A -----------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U6.5 t=U6.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U6.5 t=U6.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U6.5 t=U6.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R26.2 b=R26.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A26,J1.B26 b=J1.A27 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R11.2 b=R11.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R15.2 b=R15.1\n\n; ---- CH7 : U7, R3/R7, SET R23, J1 A28/B28, gnd A29, buf U16B -------------\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U7.5 t=U7.9\n!padne CURRENT i=3mA   f=U7.5 t=U7.6\n!padne CURRENT i=0.3mA f=U7.5 t=U7.10\n!padne RESISTANCE r=5000 a=R23.2 b=R23.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=800 a=J1.A28,J1.B28 b=J1.A29 coupling=0.001\n!padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=R3.2 b=R3.1\n!padne RESISTANCE r=20000  a=R7.2 b=R7.1\n\n; ============================================================================\n; OPTIONAL - DAC output traces.  DISABLED BY DEFAULT.\n; Only enable AFTER confirming the block above solves cleanly (no\n; \"Matrix is exactly singular\" warning). Each DACx net is given a resistive\n; path to ground (the XTR200 input impedance) so its potential is DEFINED,\n; then a current is injected from the DAC supply. Do NOT add a second\n; current source that merely removes the same current at the XTR pin -\n; that is what made v2 singular.\n; Set r= to the XTR200's real input resistance and i= accordingly.\n; Verified crossover: U20.2->U1  U20.11->U0  U20.3->U3  U20.10->U2\n;                     U20.4->U5  U20.9 ->U4  U20.5->U7  U20.8 ->U6\n; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.2  b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.2\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.11 b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.11\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.3  b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.3\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.10 b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.10\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.4  b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.4\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.9  b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.9\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.5  b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.5\n; !padne RESISTANCE r=100000 a=U20.8  b=U20.6\n; !padne CURRENT i=25uA f=U20.7 t=U20.8\n\n; ============================================================================\n; NOT MODELLED (deliberately)\n;   C1-C25 / all decoupling       - capacitors carry no DC current\n;   C26-C33 (100nF AA filter)     - likewise, no DC\n;   R28-R35 (1k, buffer -> AD7193 AIN) - the OPA2333 followers drive them\n;                                   into AD7193 analog inputs whose bias\n;                                   current is pA-level, so DC through these\n;                                   1k resistors is ~0 and their IR drop is\n;                                   unmeasurable. Adding them as RESISTANCE\n;                                   would only create CHx_V islands with no\n;                                   DC reference. If you ever want the AIN\n;                                   path modelled, add BOTH the resistor and\n;                                   a real AIN bias current, or CHx_V floats.\n;   D1 + R17 (500R, fault LED)    - R17 sits between the LED anode and the\n;                                   XTR_OD open-drain fault flag, which is\n;                                   inactive in normal operation, so DC is 0\n;                                   unless a channel is faulted. (Older note\n;                                   here said \"reverse-connected, R17=100k\" -\n;                                   that was the pre-2026-08 wiring/value.)\n;   XTR_OD, SPI, CS, PRSNT, '165  - logic nets, negligible DC\n;\n; TROUBLESHOOTING\n;   \"Matrix is exactly singular\" / NaN  -> some net has current injected but\n;       no resistive path to a reference. Every CURRENT must ultimately drain\n;       through a RESISTANCE (or land on a net a VOLTAGE source defines).\n;   \"Ground node current is not zero (X A)\" -> a loop is unterminated; X tells\n;       you the size of the offending source. X is mesh-independent when it is\n;       a directive bug (it was exactly 505 uA = the un-sourced VREF load\n;       before the REF5030 VOLTAGE source above was added).\n;   12V solving with ~0.0 uV spread and a 3.3 V reference offset -> the finger\n;       pads meshed as isolated islands; fall back to:\n;         !padne VOLTAGE v=12  p=12V0.1 n=C25.2\n;         !padne VOLTAGE v=3.3 p=3V3.1  n=C24.2\n; ============================================================================"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at -129.54 151.13 0)
